{title: Seven Days Silent}
{subtitle: Job 2:11–13; 4:1–17; 5:1–27; 15:1–35; 22:1–30; 42:7–8}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×19

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Eliphaz the Temanite [C]came from [Dm]afar
With [Bb]Bildad [C]and Zophar to meet you [Dm]there
They [Bb]looked from a distance, could [C]not recog[Dm]nize you
[Bb]Wept aloud, tore robes, [C]tossed dust to the [Dm]sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They sat with you on the [C]ground for [Dm]seven days
[Bb]And seven nights, no [C]word spoken [Dm]in praise
[Bb]Your suffering was [C]great, they saw [Dm]your pain
[Bb]Silent witness[C]es [Am7]to your deep dis[Dm]tress
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Seven days [Bb]si[C]lent, no word was [Dm]said
Watching [Bb]the sor[C]row that you have [Dm]spread
Your friends are [Bb]here, though [C]their words may [Dm]fail
To comfort the [Bb]soul [C]in the dark and [Dm]cold
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Then Eliphaz spoke, [C]who can hold [Dm]back
When [Bb]trouble strikes and the [C]body is [Dm]weak
You [Bb]strengthened the [C]weak, held [Dm]up the stumbling
[Bb]But now you are [C]dis[Am7]mayed, your spirit [Dm]crumbling
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]He spoke of a vision, [C]a spirit [Dm]passed by
[Bb]A whisper in the dark, a [C]voice [Dm]from the sky
[Bb]Who ever perished be[C]ing inno[Dm]cent
[Bb]Where were the up[C]right [Am7]ever de[Dm]stroyed
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
He accused you of sin, [C]of tak[Dm]ing pledges
Of re[Bb]fusing water, of [C]hiding [Dm]treasures
But [Bb]God spoke from the storm, [C]rebuked [Dm]them all
For [Bb]not speaking right[C]ly [Am7]of His own [Dm]will
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Offer [Bb]seven [C]bulls, [Dm]seven [Bb]rams [C]as [Dm]well
Job [Bb]prays [C]for [Dm]you, God for[C]gives your [Dm]soul
{end_of_verse}

